# XCU stty
# Copyright (c) 2026 Nicholas Martin. All rights reserved.
#
# The tests run stty on a private pseudo-terminal (core/pcpty.c), so no real
# terminal is changed.

assertion  XCU.stty.001
anchor     utilities/stty.html#DESCRIPTION
anchor     utilities/stty.html#OPTIONS
anchor     utilities/stty.html#OPERANDS
anchor     utilities/stty.html#STDOUT
class      untestable
says       The baud-rate operands (a number, ispeed, ospeed) set the line
           speed.
reason     A pseudo-terminal has no line speed or modem lines to observe, and
           the page leaves the result of failed control-mode changes
           unspecified.

assertion  XCU.stty.002
anchor     utilities/stty.html#STDOUT
anchor     utilities/stty.html#OPTIONS
class      required
since      1992
says       stty -a writes, for the terminal on standard input, each control
           character as name = value; for eof, eol, erase, intr, kill, quit,
           susp, start and stop, a speed line, and every mode operand as itself
           or with a leading minus, and a character size.
test       t/002-report-all.sh

assertion  XCU.stty.003
anchor     utilities/stty.html#STDOUT
class      required
since      1992
says       stty with no options or operands exits zero and writes a report.
test       t/003-default-report.sh

assertion  XCU.stty.004
anchor     utilities/stty.html#OPTIONS
class      required
since      1992
says       stty -g writes one line of portable printable characters with no white
           space or pathname-expansion characters, and giving that string back as
           the one argument restores the settings.
test       t/004-save-restore.sh

assertion  XCU.stty.005
anchor     utilities/stty.html#OPERANDS
class      required
since      1992
says       The input, output (base) and local mode operands set the mode and
           their minus forms clear it, as shown by -a; the control modes do the
           same when the line accepts them.
test       t/005-boolean-modes.sh

assertion  XCU.stty.006
anchor     utilities/stty.html#OPERANDS
class      required
since      1992
says       A control-character operand given a single character, undef or ^- is
           applied (the first as that character, the others as disabled), and the
           circumflex forms equal the literal control character, in either case.
test       t/006-control-chars.sh

assertion  XCU.stty.007
anchor     utilities/stty.html#OPERANDS
class      required
since      1992
says       The min and time operands change the non-canonical read parameters and
           are restored by giving the earlier values.
test       t/007-min-time.sh

assertion  XCU.stty.008
anchor     utilities/stty.html#OPERANDS
class      required
since      1992
says       evenp, parity, oddp, -parity, -evenp, -oddp, nl, -nl, ek and sane act
           as the page defines.
test       t/008-combination-modes.sh

assertion  XCU.stty.009
anchor     utilities/stty.html#OPERANDS
anchor     utilities/stty.html#STDOUT
class      required
since      2024
says       rows and cols change the window size, size writes rows, a space and
           columns, and operands that are not queries write nothing.
test       t/009-window-size.sh

assertion  XCU.stty.010
anchor     utilities/stty.html#OPERANDS
anchor     utilities/stty.html#EXIT STATUS
class      required
since      1992
says       hup is equivalent to hupcl, and an unknown operand or option is an
           error with a nonzero status and no standard output.
test       t/010-hup-and-errors.sh

assertion  XCU.stty.011
anchor     utilities/stty.html#OPERANDS
class      conditional
when       XSI
since      1992
says       The XSI output-mode operands (onlcr, ocrnl, onocr, onlret, ofill,
           ofdel and their minus forms) and the delay-style operands, with tabs
           equal to tab0 and -tabs to tab3, take effect as shown by -a.
test       t/011-xsi-output-modes.sh

assertion  XCU.stty.012
anchor     utilities/stty.html#OPERANDS
class      conditional
when       XSI
since      1992
says       raw gives cs8, -opost and -inpck, equals the operand list the page
           gives for it, and -raw equals cooked.
test       t/012-xsi-raw.sh
